    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a per-day owner creation limit that rejects creating an owner once 100 or more owners have already been registered today (by `registrationDate`), returning HTTP **429 Too Many Requests**. Changes follow the existing `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` pattern:\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `service/DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java` with `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100`.\n\n2. **Service enforcement** \u2014 in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, added a check (for new owners) that throws the exception when `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate.now()) >= 100`, plus a `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate)` helper that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` matches today (same `findAll().stream()` idiom as the city-count helper).\n\n3. **REST mapping** \u2014 in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, added an `@ExceptionHandler` mapping `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` to `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429), with the same `ProblemDetail` response shape as the sibling handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (create 100, 101st rejected with 429) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
