    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing patterns:\n\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` is a faithful sibling of `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` \u2014 same package, same `MAX_*` constant convention, same message-building style, same service-layer-invariant rationale in the javadoc.\n- `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate)` mirrors the existing private `countOwnersInCity` / `countNamesakes` helpers exactly (same `ownerRepository.findAll().stream().filter(...).count()` idiom, same \"already exist (before this create)\" javadoc phrasing). It lives in the right unit next to the other count helpers.\n- The guard in `saveOwner` is placed consistently alongside the other `owner.isNew() && count... >= MAX` checks, in a sensible order.\n- The `ExceptionControllerAdvice` handler is a direct copy of the surrounding handler shape (logging, `detailBuild`, `ResponseEntity.status(...)`), differing only in the 429 status the spec requires.\n\nNothing is duplicated beyond the deliberate parallel structure, and no class is becoming a catch-all. A maintainer of this codebase would find it natural.",
